Title: Root Markdown File Organization

Rule:
- Do not leave ad‑hoc or temporary .md files at the repository root.
- If the file is actual product/feature documentation, place it under:
  - technical-documentation/modules/<your-module-name>.md
  - Use the existing module documentation convention and keep it technical and concise.
- If the file is a temporary note, scratchpad, or work-in-progress that should not ship:
  - Put it inside a local/ directory at the repo root. This folder must remain in .gitignore.
- Keep the root directory clean; avoid creating additional top-level .md files.

Scope:
- Applies to all contributors when adding or restructuring documentation or notes.

Rationale:
- Keeps the project root tidy and makes official documentation easy to discover.
- Prevents accidental commits of transient notes by keeping them in an ignored local/ folder.
